~ start
ShopKeeper: Hi there! How can I help you today?

- Buy Items => buy_menu
- Sell Items => sell_menu
- End the conversation => END


~ buy_menu
ShopKeeper: Sure thing. What would you like to buy?

<<if GameState.coins >= 50>>
- Legendary Sword
	ShopKeeper: You bought the Legendary Sword!
	<<set GameState.coins = GameState.coins - 50>>
	<<GameState.inventory.append("Legendary Sword")>>
	=> start
<<else>>
ShopKeeper: You don’t have enough gold.
=> start
<</if>>

<<if GameState.coins >= 20>>
- Medicine
	ShopKeeper: You bought Medicine!
	<<set GameState.coins -= 20>>
	=> start
<<else>>
ShopKeeper: You don’t have enough gold.
=> start
<</if>>


~ sell_menu
ShopKeeper: What would you like to sell?

<<if "Legendary Sword" in GameState.inventory>>
- Legendary Sword
	ShopKeeper: Thanks! I’ll take that.
	<<set GameState.coins += 25>>
	<<set GameState.inventory.remove_item("Legendary Sword")>>
	=> start
<</if>>

<<if "Medicine" in GameState.inventory>>
- Medicine
	ShopKeeper: Thanks! I’ll take that.
	<<set GameState.coins += 10>>
	<<set GameState.inventory.remove_item("Medicine")>>
	=> start
<</if>>

<<if not ("Legendary Sword" in GameState.inventory or "Medicine" in GameState.inventory)>>
ShopKeeper: You have no items to sell.
=> start
<</if>>
